From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Chuang <rw0124336@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:07:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 10235: Decompiler: keep register-save stack slots mapped when
 a direct pointer escapes (#9728)

Decompiler: keep register-save stack slots mapped when a
 direct pointer escapes

Some ARM compilers (IAR, Keil MDK) allocate locals with "push {r7,lr}"
instead of "sub sp". ActionRestrictLocal marked the slot as unmapped
register-save storage, so it was treated as unaliased and a stored constant
was propagated across a call that receives a pointer to the slot.

Leave the slot mapped when a pointer with a constant offset from the stack
pointer (no variable index) points into it. Adds datatest escapedstackslot.xml.

Fixes #9728
